// The boundary of the self-less slot channel, pinned from the other side. The slot is filled from
// the CALL's instantiation, so a self-less member whose result says nothing about `T` leaves nothing
// to fill it from: `Repo.label()` returns `string`, no argument mentions `T`, and no annotation can
// reach it. That is E0023 at **check** time — not a silent `"dyn"`, and not a run-time abort.
//
// The help matters as much as the code. A method's `::<…>` names the METHOD's own type parameters,
// never its class's (those come from the receiver's type arguments), so "supply it explicitly" is a
// dead end here and the message says the thing that does work instead.
// expect: error E0023 at 21:6
// expect: exit 1
struct Todo {
    id: int
}
class Repo<T> {
    pub tbl: string

    fn label(): string {
        return type_name::<T>();
    }
}
echo Repo.label();
